Patch 7915 (experimental, rollback netcode): canonical pad record hook, pad-info hook and a delivered-vblank counter, for the rollback stepper.

g_cellpad_canon_hook(port, button, len, setting_len, host_connected) runs at the end of cellPadGetData, after the host layer and the 6501
filters built the record, and may replace it whole (len and button[]). The stepper (installer/port/jsp/jsp_stepper.cpp) uses it to hand
the game the same bytes on every machine and to give a replayed tick its recorded input instead of a fresh device read.
g_cellpad_info_hook(info) runs in cellPadGetInfo2 on the host CellPadInfo2, before the copy to guest memory (the stepper reports the session's slots as
connected with it). libs/input/cellPad.h declares both hooks with the toolkit's types, so a port includes the header instead of redeclaring them.
cellGcm_vblank_delivered() counts the vblank notifications the GCM pump delivered to the guest: two back-to-back cellGcmTickVBlank calls
coalesce into one pending bit, so the replay clock waits for this counter after each tick.
All hooks NULL by default; the counter is always counted (one increment per delivered vblank) and unread unless the port reads it
(only with JSP_ROLLBACK=1). No behaviour change until the port sets the hooks.

